meta {
  name: Post places within (lookup)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/places/within
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "lat": 41.3874,
    "lon": 2.1686,
    "mode": "pedestrian",
    "minutes": 10
  }
}

docs {
  Counts Overture Places (POIs) inside a previously computed isochrone contour,
  looked up by point/mode/minutes rather than passing the polygon directly.

  Body (lookup mode):
  - `lat` float, required, -90..90
  - `lon` float, required, -180..180
  - `mode` string, required, one of `pedestrian` | `auto`
  - `minutes` int, required, one of `5 | 10 | 15` (matches `CONTOUR_MINUTES`)

  Requires `/isochrone` to have been called first for this exact `lat/lon/mode`
  (same rounding as the isochrone cache key) — the polygon is read from the
  Redis cache, not recomputed. If not cached, 404.

  See "Post places within (polygon)" for passing geometry directly instead.

  Response:
  {
    "total": number,
    "types": [{ "type": string, "count": number }],
    "categories": [{ "category": string, "type": string, "count": number }]
  }

  - `categories` = raw Overture `categories.primary` values (fine-grained, e.g. `tapas_bar`)
  - `types` = counts grouped by Overture's own `basic_category` field (coarser, e.g. `restaurant`, `bar`, `hotel`)
  - Only places with `confidence >= OVERTURE_MIN_CONFIDENCE` (default 0.6) are counted

  Errors:
  - 400 coordinate/polygon outside Catalonia bbox
  - 404 no cached isochrone for this lat/lon/mode, or no contour matching `minutes`
  - 422 missing/invalid input (must provide either `geometry` or full `lat/lon/mode/minutes`)
}
